[366.521397, "o", "\r                                        \r\r\nI have completed the research phase for `ntfy` version `v2.19.2`. I checked the upstream documentation and repository, verified there are no existing `ntfy` charms on Charmhub, and synthesised a design proposal.\r\n\r\nHere is the design for your review:\r\n\r\n### Substrate and Path\r\n* **Platform:** Kubernetes (K8s)\r\n* **Architecture:** Path A (12-factor application) using the `go-framework` profile and `paas-charm`. Since `ntfy` is a stateless Go service (when backed by Postgres), it perfectly fits the 12-factor model.\r\n\r\n### Integrations (Relations)\r\n* **Ingress (`ingress`)**: For public access, likely via Traefik.\r\n* **Database (`postgresql_client`)**: When related, `ntfy` uses PostgreSQL for caching messages, managing users, and handling web push subscriptions. This implicitly enables authentication and access control, making the charm HA-ready out of the box.\r\n* **Observability (`cos_agent`)**: Automatic integration with the Canonical Observability Stack (Grafana, Prometheus, Loki) through the 12-factor base.\r\n\r\n### Config Options\r\n* `base_url`: Public-facing base URL of the service (required for iOS push, attachments, and emails).\r\n* `behind_proxy`: Defaults to `true` (critical for rate limiting per client IP when behind an ingress controller).\r\n* `cache_duration`: Duration for which messages will be buffered (e.g., `12h`).\r\n* `attachment_total_size_limit`: Limit of the on-disk attachment cache directory.\r\n* `attachment_file_size_limit`: Per-file attachment size limit.\r\n* `attachment_expiry_duration`: Duration after which uploaded attachments are deleted.\r\n\r\n### Open Questions\r\n1. **Attachment Storage for HA:** By default, attachments are stored on disk. If we scale `ntfy` to multiple units, attachments will be fragmented across pods. `ntfy` supports S3 for attachment storage. **Should we add an S3 integration (`s3` interface) so attachments are shared across all units if you choose to scale horizontally?**\r\n\r\nLet me know if this design looks good to you, or if you'd like to adjust the integrations, add the S3 relation, or change any of the config options!\r\n\r\n"]
[366.526742, "o", "> "]
